+opinion or a declaration of copyright ownership.
+
+## Evidence available
+
+- Git remote `origin` points to `https://github.com/Spamziesagcan/updatis`.
+- The inspected history contains commits under `Spamziesagcan
+  <harshchandramania@gmail.com>` and `Harsh Chandramania
+  <142709378+Spamziesagcan@users.noreply.github.com>`.
+- The similar GitHub identity suggests a relationship, but Git author metadata
+  can be configured by anyone and does not establish ownership or the right to
+  relicense every contribution.
+- No tracked `LICENSE`, contributor agreement, or third-party notice file was
+  found at the Foundation baseline.
+
+Therefore repository ownership and authority to adopt Apache 2.0 remain
+**unresolved**. The Foundation gate does not add a license or claim that the
+repository is already distributable under Apache 2.0. Rights holders must
+confirm provenance and licensing before a public licensing claim.
+
+## Frontend status
+
+`nextjs-order-dashboard` is a Git gitlink at object
+`e4ee74b6fda3825cfc6165a91ce5471f3855bed4`, but the repository has no
+`.gitmodules` mapping. The object is also an earlier commit in this repository
+and contains an order-dashboard tree. This unusual self-referential historical
+state is not a usable, reproducible submodule checkout and supplies no separate
+license evidence.
+
+No frontend files are restored, copied, regenerated, or treated as product
+assets by the Foundation gate. Tests, contracts, and CI are frontend
+independent. A future dashboard starts only after provenance is resolved or is
+implemented independently under an established project license.
+
+The historical frontend and current MySQL order application are legacy
+examples. Neither establishes supported MySQL product compatibility.
